  "lang": "en",
  "description": [
    "The harmonic mean is a kind of mean which is calculated by dividing the total number of observations by the reciprocal of each number in a series.\n\nHarmonic Mean = N/(1/a1+1/a2+1/a3+1/a4+.......+1/aN)  \nwhere a(i)= Individual score and  N = Sample size (Number of scores)"
  ],
  "synonyms": [],
  "annotation": {
